export const DATA_83: ReadingTest[] = [
  { id: "rd-125", num: 125, title: "Đề 125", timeMin: 60, parts: [
    { title: "Everyday Actions for a Healthier Planet", paragraphs: ["In recent years, concern about the state of the natural environment has grown significantly among people of all ages and backgrounds. Climate change, plastic pollution, deforestation, and the loss of wildlife habitats are no longer distant problems discussed only by scientists and policymakers — they are issues that affect everyday life in visible and increasingly urgent ways. As a result, more and more individuals around the world are choosing to make changes in their daily routines in order to reduce the harm they cause to the planet. These changes range from small personal habits to active participation in community campaigns, and together they form part of a growing global movement toward more environmentally responsible living.", "One of the most widely practised forms of environmental action is reducing waste, particularly plastic waste. Single-use plastics such as straws, plastic bags, and disposable cups have become a major source of pollution in oceans and rivers, harming marine animals and contaminating water supplies. In response, many people have switched to reusable alternatives — carrying their own shopping bags, using metal or bamboo straws, and bringing refillable water bottles instead of buying bottled water. Some cities and countries have gone further by introducing legislation that bans or taxes single-use plastics, encouraging businesses and consumers alike to find more sustainable options. While these legal measures have faced some resistance from industries that rely on plastic production, studies in several countries have shown that they significantly reduce plastic consumption within a relatively short period after implementation.", "Reducing energy consumption at home is another area where individuals can make a meaningful difference. Heating and cooling systems, electrical appliances, and lighting together account for a substantial proportion of household energy use, much of which is still generated from fossil fuels that release carbon dioxide into the atmosphere. Simple actions such as turning off lights when leaving a room, unplugging devices that are not in use, and adjusting thermostats to avoid unnecessary heating or cooling can collectively reduce a household's energy footprint. Many households have also invested in energy-efficient appliances or installed solar panels on their rooftops, reducing their dependence on grid electricity and in some cases generating surplus energy that can be sold back to the power network. Governments in many countries offer subsidies or tax incentives to encourage these investments, recognising that widespread adoption of cleaner energy technology at the household level is an important part of national climate strategies.", "Transportation is one of the largest contributors to greenhouse gas emissions globally, and changing how people travel is therefore one of the most impactful choices an individual can make. In urban areas, choosing to walk, cycle, or use public transport instead of driving a private car can substantially reduce a person's carbon footprint. Car-sharing schemes and the growing availability of electric vehicles offer additional options for those who cannot easily give up personal vehicle use. Beyond individual choices, many cities are investing in cycling infrastructure, pedestrian zones, and expanded public transport networks, making it progressively easier for residents to choose lower-emission forms of travel. Employers in some countries have introduced incentive programmes that reward staff for commuting by bicycle or public transport, reflecting a recognition that sustainable travel habits are shaped not only by personal values but also by the practical options that urban environments make available.", "Community-level environmental action has proven particularly effective in creating lasting change. Neighbourhood clean-up campaigns, tree-planting initiatives, and local conservation projects engage residents in hands-on activities that not only improve the immediate environment but also strengthen social bonds and raise awareness of broader ecological issues. Schools and universities have become important sites for environmental education, with many institutions introducing sustainability programmes that teach students about the science of climate change, the importance of biodiversity, and the practical skills needed to live more sustainably. Youth-led movements such as the global school climate strikes, inspired in part by the activism of Swedish campaigner Greta Thunberg, have demonstrated that young people are increasingly willing to demand systemic change rather than simply adapting their personal habits.", "Despite the genuine enthusiasm that many people feel for environmental action, experts caution that individual behaviour change alone is insufficient to address the scale of the ecological crises facing the planet. The most significant drivers of environmental damage — industrial agriculture, fossil fuel extraction, and large-scale manufacturing — operate at a level of complexity and economic power that personal choices cannot easily influence. Critics of what is sometimes called the \"individual responsibility\" model of environmentalism argue that placing the burden of environmental protection on consumers deflects attention from the systemic reforms that corporations and governments must undertake. This perspective does not dismiss the value of individual action but insists that personal behaviour change must be accompanied by ambitious policy reform, corporate accountability, and international cooperation if meaningful progress is to be achieved at the scale the crisis demands."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main idea of the passage?", options: ["Reducing plastic waste is the single most important environmental action that individuals can take, and legislation banning single-use plastics has proven to be the most successful policy tool.", "Governments and corporations bear the sole responsibility for solving environmental problems, and individual actions are too small to make any meaningful difference.", "People around the world are taking a variety of actions to protect the environment, though experts warn that individual efforts alone cannot address the full scale of ecological crises.", "The most effective way to combat climate change is through youth activism and school-based environmental education programmes that inspire the next generation of policymakers."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following best describes how many individuals have responded to the problem of plastic pollution?", options: ["They have focused on recycling existing plastic waste more efficiently rather than changing their purchasing habits or reducing the amount of plastic they use.", "They have joined formal campaigns lobbying governments to impose immediate total bans on all forms of plastic packaging used in the food and retail industries.", "They have switched to reusable alternatives such as their own shopping bags, metal or bamboo straws, and refillable water bottles in their daily lives.", "They have reduced plastic use primarily by purchasing products from companies that have voluntarily committed to eliminating plastic from their supply chains."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what is one benefit that households with solar panels may gain beyond reducing their own energy consumption?", options: ["They gain access to preferential electricity rates from energy providers who reward customers for investing in renewable energy generation technology.", "They are exempted from paying local environmental taxes, which are typically levied on households that continue to rely entirely on grid-supplied electricity.", "They become eligible for government-funded home improvement grants that cover the full cost of additional energy-efficiency upgrades to their property.", "They can generate surplus electricity that may be sold back to the power network, effectively turning their home into a small-scale energy producer."], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"subsidies\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["penalty charges applied to households that exceed a specified threshold of energy consumption during peak demand periods", "legally binding requirements imposed on households to adopt specific energy-saving technologies within a government-mandated timeframe", "financial support provided by governments to reduce the cost of particular investments or activities that are considered beneficial to society", "voluntary contributions made by private companies to fund public awareness campaigns promoting household energy efficiency"], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what distinguishes youth-led environmental movements from other forms of individual environmental action described in the passage?", options: ["Youth movements focus exclusively on raising funds for scientific research into renewable energy technologies rather than changing personal consumption habits.", "Rather than simply modifying personal habits, young activists have shown a willingness to demand large-scale systemic change through public protest and political pressure.", "Youth-led campaigns have been more successful than adult-led initiatives because they receive greater media coverage and attract more international financial support.", "Young activists tend to prioritise local conservation projects such as tree planting and neighbourhood clean-ups over broader political or policy-focused campaigns."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a lower-emission travel option available to urban residents?", options: ["Walking or cycling instead of using a private car for everyday journeys within the city.", "Taking advantage of electric vehicles for those who need to maintain access to personal transport.", "Using car-sharing schemes that allow multiple people to share a single vehicle and split travel costs.", "Booking intercity high-speed rail services as an alternative to short-haul domestic air travel."], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"these\" in paragraph 2 refers to _______.", options: ["the studies conducted in several countries to evaluate the effectiveness of policies aimed at reducing plastic waste in the short term", "the legal measures such as bans and taxes on single-use plastics that governments have introduced to reduce plastic consumption", "the single-use plastic products such as straws, bags, and disposable cups that have become a major source of ocean and river pollution worldwide", "the businesses and consumers who have faced pressure to find more sustainable packaging alternatives as public awareness of plastic pollution has grown"], answer: 1 }, { q: "The word \"deflects\" in paragraph 6 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["moderates and balances, by ensuring that responsibility for solving a problem is distributed fairly among all the parties that have contributed to it", "reinforces and strengthens, by drawing greater public and political attention to an issue that might otherwise receive insufficient scrutiny", "diverts or redirects away from something, causing focus or responsibility to shift toward a different target than the one most deserving of attention", "eliminates entirely, by replacing one framework of understanding with another that is more accurate and more useful for guiding effective action"], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as an example of community-level environmental action?", options: ["Fundraising drives organised by community groups to donate money to international environmental protection organisations.", "Neighbourhood clean-up campaigns that bring local residents together to remove waste from public spaces.", "Tree-planting initiatives and local conservation projects that improve the immediate environment and raise ecological awareness.", "School and university sustainability programmes that educate students about climate science and practical skills for sustainable living."], answer: 0 }, { q: "What is the most likely reason the author includes the argument about \"individual responsibility\" in the final paragraph?", options: ["To provide a more complete and balanced perspective by acknowledging the limits of personal behaviour change and the need for systemic reform alongside individual action.", "To argue that individual environmental actions are entirely ineffective and that people should focus their energy exclusively on political advocacy and corporate campaigning.", "To criticise environmental activists for focusing too much on large-scale policy change and neglecting the practical everyday habits that ordinary people can realistically adopt.", "To conclude that the environmental movement has failed because it has been unable to convince governments and corporations to take the ambitious action that the crisis requires."], answer: 0 }] },
    { title: "Artificial Intelligence in Education: Promise, Tension, and the Road Ahead", paragraphs: ["The integration of artificial intelligence into educational settings has emerged as one of the most actively debated developments in contemporary pedagogy. Proponents of AI-assisted learning argue that intelligent technologies offer unprecedented opportunities to personalise instruction, identify learning difficulties at an early stage, and extend quality education to students in regions where qualified teachers are in short supply. Sceptics, meanwhile, raise concerns about data privacy, algorithmic bias, the erosion of the teacher-student relationship, and the risk that an over-reliance on automated systems may ultimately narrow rather than enrich the educational experience. Between these competing visions lies a more nuanced reality: AI is already reshaping classrooms around the world, but the outcomes of that reshaping depend enormously on the intentions, resources, and values of the institutions that deploy these technologies and the communities they serve.", "The most widely adopted AI applications in education to date have focused on adaptive learning platforms — software systems that adjust the difficulty, pace, and content of instructional material in response to each student's performance in real time. Unlike a traditional classroom in which a single teacher must simultaneously address the needs of thirty or more students with varying levels of prior knowledge and ability, an adaptive platform can provide each learner with a tailored sequence of tasks, immediate feedback on errors, and targeted practice in areas where performance data indicates weakness. Companies such as Khan Academy, Duolingo, and Carnegie Learning have developed platforms that use machine learning algorithms to model individual learner trajectories and predict which types of exercises are most likely to consolidate understanding at each stage of a student's progress. Research evaluating these platforms has produced mixed results: some studies report significant improvements in standardised test scores and student engagement, while others find that gains are modest and that motivated students benefit disproportionately, raising concerns about equity.", "Beyond adaptive learning, AI is increasingly being used to support teachers rather than replace them — a distinction that many educators consider pivotal . Automated essay scoring systems can provide students with rapid formative feedback on written work, freeing teachers from the time-consuming burden of grading routine assignments and allowing them to focus on higher-order instructional tasks such as facilitating discussion, mentoring individual students, and designing creative learning experiences. Natural language processing tools can analyse patterns in classroom discourse, flagging moments where student engagement drops or where particular explanations appear to generate persistent confusion. Administrative AI applications automate scheduling, attendance tracking, and progress reporting, reducing the bureaucratic workload that many teachers identify as one of the primary sources of professional stress and burnout. Taken together, these applications represent an attempt to use technology to restore to teachers the time and cognitive bandwidth that administrative demands have progressively eroded.", "The deployment of AI in education raises significant ethical questions that the rapid pace of technological development has often outrun. The collection of granular data on student behaviour, performance, and even emotional states — enabled by tools that track eye movements, keystroke patterns, and facial expressions — represents a form of surveillance that many privacy advocates argue is disproportionate and potentially harmful. Children and adolescents, who cannot meaningfully consent to the collection and commercial use of their personal data, are particularly vulnerable to exploitation by edtech companies whose business models may prioritise engagement metrics and data monetisation over genuine educational outcomes. Several jurisdictions, including the European Union under its General Data Protection Regulation, have introduced legal frameworks that impose strict limits on the collection and use of children's data, but enforcement remains inconsistent and the technical complexity of modern AI systems makes independent auditing difficult.", "Algorithmic bias presents a related but distinct challenge. AI systems trained on historical educational data inevitably reflect the inequalities embedded in that data — patterns of underachievement associated with socioeconomic disadvantage, racial discrimination, and inadequate school funding may be encoded into predictive models that then reinforce these patterns by directing fewer resources or lower expectations toward already disadvantaged students. A system that predicts a student is unlikely to succeed in advanced mathematics based on early performance data may effectively remove that student from an enriched learning pathway before they have had the opportunity to develop the skills that the prediction purports to measure. Critics argue that this form of algorithmic determinism — the tendency of automated systems to treat statistical patterns as fixed individual destinies — represents one of the most serious risks associated with the uncritical adoption of AI in educational contexts.", "Despite these challenges, a number of initiatives around the world are demonstrating that AI can be deployed in education in ways that are genuinely equitable, transparent, and pedagogically sound. In several low- and middle-income countries, AI-powered tutoring systems have been piloted as a means of extending access to quality instruction in regions where teacher shortages are acute and school infrastructure is limited. Projects in India, Kenya, and the Philippines have used mobile-based AI tutoring applications to provide personalised mathematics and literacy instruction to students in rural communities, with early evaluations suggesting measurable improvements in foundational skills. These initiatives are not without their own challenges — unreliable internet connectivity, the cost of devices, and the need for teacher training all present implementation barriers — but they offer a counterpoint to the assumption that AI in education is primarily a phenomenon of wealthy, technologically advanced societies.", "The broader question of what role AI should play in education ultimately cannot be answered by technology alone. It requires sustained engagement with fundamental questions about the purposes of schooling — whether education is primarily about the efficient transmission of measurable skills, the cultivation of critical thinking and democratic citizenship, or the nurturing of individual human potential in ways that resist easy quantification. Different answers to these questions will lead to very different decisions about which AI applications to adopt, how to govern their use, and whose interests they should primarily serve. What the evidence suggests, above all, is that AI is a powerful but value-laden tool: its effects in educational settings will reflect not the inherent properties of the technology itself but the choices — deliberate or inadvertent — of the societies that deploy it."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main purpose of the passage?", options: ["To demonstrate that AI-powered tutoring systems in low-income countries are the most promising application of educational technology and should be prioritised for international development funding.", "To examine the opportunities, ethical challenges, and varied real-world outcomes associated with the integration of artificial intelligence into educational settings.", "To advocate for the rapid and widespread adoption of AI in classrooms worldwide, arguing that its benefits in personalising instruction far outweigh any associated risks or ethical concerns.", "To argue that the risks of algorithmic bias and data privacy violations are so severe that governments should impose strict moratoriums on the use of AI in schools."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, what do research findings on adaptive learning platforms suggest about their educational effectiveness?", options: ["The evidence overwhelmingly indicates that motivated, high-achieving students perform worse on adaptive platforms because the systems constrain their learning pace artificially.", "Research consistently shows that adaptive platforms produce large and equitable improvements in academic achievement across all student groups and socioeconomic backgrounds.", "Research has conclusively shown that adaptive platforms are effective only when used as supplementary tools outside the classroom, not as primary instructional resources.", "Studies have produced mixed results, with some reporting improvements in test scores and engagement while others find modest gains and raise concerns about equity."], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"pivotal\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["widely misunderstood and frequently overstated, particularly by technology companies seeking to justify the commercial applications they are developing for educational markets", "critically important and central to the issue, such that getting it right or wrong determines the direction and quality of what follows", "technically complex and difficult to implement consistently, requiring specialised expertise that most schools and educational institutions currently lack", "ethically ambiguous and context-dependent, meaning that its significance varies considerably depending on the cultural and institutional setting in which it is applied"], answer: 1 }, { q: "The word \"these\" in paragraph 2 refers to _______.", options: ["the standardised test scores and engagement measures used by researchers to evaluate whether AI-powered educational tools deliver meaningful academic improvements", "the machine learning algorithms that model individual learner trajectories and predict which exercises are most likely to consolidate understanding at each stage of progress", "the patterns of prior knowledge and ability that vary among students in a traditional classroom and that a single teacher must simultaneously attempt to address", "the adaptive learning platforms developed by companies such as Khan Academy, Duolingo, and Carnegie Learning that adjust instruction based on student performance"], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, why do critics consider algorithmic determinism in education particularly dangerous?", options: ["Because machine learning algorithms cannot be audited by educators or regulators, making it impossible to identify or correct errors in the predictions they generate about individual students.", "Because automated systems collect far more personal data than is necessary for their educational function, creating legal liability for schools that deploy them without parental consent.", "Because predictive models may direct fewer resources or lower expectations toward disadvantaged students, effectively reinforcing existing inequalities before students have had a fair chance to develop.", "Because algorithmic systems replace the nuanced professional judgment of experienced teachers with statistical patterns that are incapable of capturing the full complexity of human learning."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following best describes the AI education initiatives in low- and middle-income countries discussed in paragraph 6?", options: ["They have shown promising early results in improving foundational skills but face practical implementation barriers such as connectivity issues, device costs, and the need for teacher training.", "They have demonstrated that AI tutoring systems are most effective when deployed as a complete replacement for classroom instruction rather than as a supplement to existing teaching.", "They have been uniformly successful in eliminating teacher shortages and raising standardised test scores to levels comparable with those achieved in wealthier, technology-advanced nations.", "They have been criticised by international education experts for diverting funding away from proven methods such as teacher recruitment and school infrastructure investment."], answer: 0 }, { q: "The word \"granular\" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["highly detailed and fine-grained, capturing information at a very precise and specific level rather than in broad or aggregated categories", "broadly representative and statistically reliable, collected from a sufficiently large sample to support valid generalisations about a target population", "technically generated and machine-readable, processed by automated systems rather than interpreted through direct human observation or assessment", "commercially sensitive and legally protected, subject to strict restrictions on how it may be accessed, stored, or shared with third parties"], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a way in which AI applications are being used to support teachers in the classroom?", options: ["Administrative applications that handle scheduling, attendance tracking, and progress reporting to reduce the bureaucratic burden on teaching staff.", "Automated essay scoring systems that give students rapid feedback on written assignments and reduce the time teachers spend on routine grading.", "Natural language processing tools that analyse classroom discussion patterns and identify moments where student engagement drops or confusion persists.", "AI curriculum design software that autonomously plans lesson sequences and generates complete teaching materials tailored to a class's overall performance profile."], answer: 3 }, { q: "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage about the relationship between AI and educational inequality?", options: ["AI consistently benefits lower-achieving students more than higher-achieving ones because adaptive systems are specifically programmed to prioritise support for those who are falling behind.", "Educational inequality is primarily a consequence of algorithmic bias, and removing AI from schools would therefore be the most effective means of ensuring equal learning opportunities for all students.", "The effects of AI on educational equity are determined not by the technology itself but by how it is designed, trained, and deployed — and it can either reduce or reinforce existing disparities.", "AI is inherently a democratising force in education, and any inequalities that arise from its use are temporary side effects that will be resolved as the technology continues to mature."], answer: 2 }, { q: "Which of the following best describes the author's view of who bears ultimate responsibility for the outcomes of AI in education?", options: ["Societies and institutions, because the values, choices, and governance frameworks that humans bring to the deployment of AI ultimately determine its effects more than the technology itself.", "Technology companies, because they design and profit from AI systems and therefore have both the capability and the obligation to ensure that their products cause no harm to students.", "Individual teachers, because their daily instructional decisions determine whether AI tools are used in ways that genuinely support learning or simply automate existing inequalities.", "Regulatory bodies, because only independent government oversight can provide the enforcement mechanisms necessary to prevent the misuse of AI data and the perpetuation of algorithmic bias."], answer: 0 }] },
    { title: "The Science of Staying Healthy: Beyond Diet and Exercise", paragraphs: ["For decades, public health messaging has revolved around two central pillars: eat well and exercise regularly. While neither of these recommendations is misguided, a growing body of research suggests that the determinants of long-term health are considerably more complex than this familiar refrain implies. Scientists and epidemiologists are now examining a broader constellation of factors — from sleep quality and social connection to chronic stress and environmental exposure — that collectively shape an individual's risk of disease and their capacity for recovery. [1] Understanding these factors does not diminish the importance of diet and physical activity; rather, it situates them within a richer and more accurate picture of human health.", "One of the most compelling areas of emerging research concerns the role of sleep. Historically treated as a passive state of rest, sleep is now understood to be a period of intense biological activity. During deep sleep phases, the brain undergoes a process sometimes called \"synaptic pruning,\" in which neural connections are selectively strengthened or eliminated based on the day's learning and experience. Simultaneously, the glymphatic system — a network of channels surrounding the brain's blood vessels — becomes significantly more active, flushing out metabolic waste products including proteins associated with neurodegenerative conditions such as Alzheimer's disease. Adults who consistently sleep fewer than seven hours per night show measurably elevated levels of inflammatory markers, impaired glucose regulation, and reduced immune response. [2] These findings have led many researchers to argue that sleep deprivation should be treated as a public health crisis on par with obesity and physical inactivity.", "Social connection represents another domain that has historically been undervalued in health discourse. Decades of longitudinal studies — most notably the Harvard Study of Adult Development, which tracked participants for over eighty years — have demonstrated that the quality of a person's relationships is among the strongest predictors of both mental and physical health outcomes. Individuals who report high levels of loneliness show patterns of chronic low-grade inflammation similar to those observed in heavy smokers, a finding that has prompted some researchers to describe social isolation as being \"as damaging as smoking fifteen cigarettes a day.\" The mechanisms linking social bonds to physical health are not yet fully elucidated , but leading hypotheses point to the buffering effect that supportive relationships have on the body's stress response systems, particularly the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis. [3]", "Chronic psychological stress occupies a central position in this expanded model of health. When the body perceives a threat, it initiates a cascade of hormonal responses — most prominently the release of cortisol and adrenaline — designed to mobilize energy and sharpen attention for immediate action. This stress response evolved for short-term survival situations and is highly adaptive in that context. However, when stress becomes persistent rather than episodic, the sustained elevation of stress hormones begins to damage the cardiovascular system, suppress immune function, disrupt hormonal balance, and accelerate cellular aging through the erosion of telomeres, the protective caps at the ends of chromosomes. Research published over the past two decades has increasingly linked chronic workplace stress, financial insecurity, and caregiving burdens to significantly elevated risks of heart disease, type 2 diabetes, and depression. [4]", "Environmental factors add yet another dimension to this picture. Exposure to air pollution, particularly fine particulate matter, has been linked not only to respiratory disease but also to cardiovascular events, cognitive decline. To mitigate these risks, city planners emphasize access to green spaces, clean water, and safe neighborhoods. Although many municipal budgets neglect these critical areas, local governments must prioritize them because they exert a substantial influence on health trajectories. Epidemiologists increasingly speak of the \"social determinants of health,\" a concept that acknowledges how profoundly conditions such as income, education, housing quality, and access to healthcare shape the biological processes underlying disease. This perspective challenges the individualistic framing that dominates conventional health advice, suggesting that systemic changes may ultimately be more powerful levers for population health than any single behavioral intervention.", "None of this is to suggest that personal choices are irrelevant. Diet and exercise remain genuinely important, and there is substantial evidence that individuals can meaningfully improve their health outcomes through sustained lifestyle modification. However, the evidence also indicates that framing health exclusively as a matter of personal responsibility may obscure the structural barriers that make healthy choices harder for some populations than others. A truly comprehensive approach to public health must therefore integrate behavioral guidance with environmental reform, social policy, and equitable access to resources — recognizing that health, in the fullest sense, is as much a social and political achievement as it is a biological one."], questions: [{ q: "What is the central argument of the passage?", options: ["Social isolation poses a greater threat to public health than either poor diet or inadequate physical activity.", "Diet and regular exercise remain the most reliable predictors of long-term health outcomes for most individuals.", "Long-term health is shaped by a wide range of interconnected factors that extend well beyond diet and physical activity.", "Environmental conditions and government policy are the primary forces determining population-level health outcomes."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what function does the glymphatic system perform during sleep?", options: ["It reinforces neural pathways that were formed through learning and experience during waking hours.", "It coordinates the selective elimination of unnecessary neural connections through a process called synaptic pruning.", "It removes harmful metabolic byproducts from the brain, including proteins linked to neurodegenerative disease.", "It regulates the release of cortisol and adrenaline to prepare the body for the following day's activities."], answer: 2 }, { q: "The Harvard Study of Adult Development is cited in the passage primarily to support which claim?", options: ["Social support directly suppresses the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis's response to psychological stress.", "Longitudinal research methods are the most reliable tools available for studying the determinants of human health.", "The quality of interpersonal relationships is one of the most significant predictors of long-term health outcomes.", "Chronic low-grade inflammation is a common consequence of both social isolation and habitual tobacco use."], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"flushing\" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["actively expelling or clearing away unwanted substances from a biological system", "absorbing and neutralizing toxic proteins within surrounding brain tissue", "filtering and redistributing metabolic compounds throughout the cerebral bloodstream", "stimulating the production of protective enzymes in neural channel networks"], answer: 0 }, { q: "Which of the following square brackets [1] , [2] , [3] , or [4] best indicates where the following sentence could be added? 'These physiological disruptions are compounded further when stress becomes intertwined with social isolation, creating a mutually reinforcing cycle of biological harm.'", options: ["[1]", "[2]", "[3]", "[4]"], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, exposure to fine particulate matter has been associated with which of the following health consequences?", options: ["Accelerated telomere erosion and elevated inflammatory markers in urban populations.", "Disrupted hormonal balance and impaired glucose regulation in children and adolescents.", "Higher rates of cardiovascular disease, cognitive decline, and negative outcomes at birth.", "Increased vulnerability to infectious diseases and reduced effectiveness of vaccination programs."], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"them\" in paragraph 5 refers to _______.", options: ["municipal budgets", "respiratory diseases", "city planners", "green spaces, clean water, and safe neighborhoods"], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"elucidated\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["thoroughly validated through controlled experimental studies and peer review", "widely accepted as established fact within the mainstream scientific community", "fully understood or explained in a clear and comprehensive manner", "formally published in internationally recognized academic journals"], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a consequence of chronic psychological stress?", options: ["Damage to the cardiovascular system due to sustained elevation of stress hormones.", "Impairment of the glymphatic system's ability to clear metabolic waste from the brain.", "Disruption of the body's hormonal balance and suppression of immune function.", "Acceleration of cellular aging through deterioration of chromosomal protective structures."], answer: 1 }, { q: "What can be inferred about the author's attitude toward conventional public health advice focused on individual behavior?", options: ["The author views individual behavioral guidance as useful but insufficient without addressing broader social and systemic conditions.", "The author argues that personal responsibility for health should be replaced entirely by government-led public health interventions.", "The author believes individual behavioral choices are irrelevant when structural and environmental barriers are present.", "The author considers conventional health advice to be fundamentally incorrect and in need of complete revision."], answer: 0 }] },
    { title: "The Endurance and Evolution of Chinese Traditional Festivals", paragraphs: ["Among the many dimensions of Chinese civilization that have attracted sustained scholarly attention, the system of traditional festivals occupies a particularly revealing position. These occasions — ranging from the grand spectacle of the Lunar New Year to the more contemplative observances of the Qingming festival — are far more than calendrical markers or occasions for communal festivity. They represent a condensed expression of cosmological beliefs, agricultural knowledge, filial obligations, and collective memory that has been transmitted, adapted, and contested across more than two millennia. [1] To study Chinese traditional festivals is, in many respects, to engage with the question of how a civilization sustains cultural continuity in the face of transformative historical rupture.", "The Lunar New Year, known in Mandarin as Chūnjié or the Spring Festival, stands as the most widely observed of these occasions, celebrated not only throughout mainland China but across the global Chinese diaspora from San Francisco to Singapore. Its ritual structure — encompassing the reunion dinner on New Year's Eve, the exchange of red envelopes (hóngbāo) containing monetary gifts, the setting off of firecrackers to dispel malevolent spirits, and the decoration of doorways with couplets expressing auspicious wishes — encodes a dense layering of symbolic meaning. The color red, ubiquitous during this period, invokes protection against the mythological creature Nian, whose annual incursions were said to be repelled by loud noise and bright light. [2] Historians of religion note that such etiological myths, whatever their literal implausibility, serve a powerful mnemonic function, binding participants to a shared narrative of origin and survival that transcends any single generation's experience.", "The Qingming festival, observed in early April approximately fifteen days after the spring equinox, presents a markedly different character. Rooted in the ancient practice of ancestor veneration, Qingming requires descendants to visit the graves of their forebears, clear away overgrowth, make offerings of food and incense, and burn paper effigies of goods believed to be needed in the afterlife. The festival's name — meaning \"pure brightness\" — alludes both to the clarity of the spring atmosphere and to the moral luminosity ascribed to the act of honoring one's ancestors. Contemporary sociologists have observed that Qingming serves a dual psychological function: it reinforces intergenerational bonds by physically reconnecting the living with sites of familial memory, while simultaneously offering a structured ritual framework through which grief and loss may be collectively processed. The growing practice of \"online grave sweeping,\" in which digital memorials are visited and virtual offerings made via smartphone applications, has provoked considerable debate about whether the essence of such rituals resides in their physical enactment or in the intention and continuity of the commemorative impulse. [3]", "The Dragon Boat Festival (Duānwǔjié), held on the fifth day of the fifth lunar month, traces its most widely cited origin to the commemoration of Qu Yuan, a minister and poet of the Warring States period who, upon being exiled following false accusations of disloyalty, drowned himself in the Miluo River in an act of principled protest. According to tradition, local people raced their boats across the water in a futile attempt at rescue, and beat drums and threw rice dumplings (zòngzi) into the river to prevent fish from consuming his body. The festival thus fuses elements of patriotic veneration, seasonal ritual, and competitive spectacle in a manner that illustrates how Chinese festivals frequently accommodate multiple, sometimes contradictory, layers of meaning simultaneously. Ethnographers have noted that origin narratives for major Chinese festivals are rarely singular: the Dragon Boat Festival, for instance, is also associated in different regional traditions with the commemoration of Wu Zixu and with apotropaic rites designed to repel the diseases and malevolent energies thought to intensify during the fifth lunar month. [4]", "The Mid-Autumn Festival (Zhōngqiūjié), celebrated on the fifteenth day of the eighth lunar month when the moon reaches its annual apogee of fullness, centers on the appreciation of the harvest moon and the sharing of mooncakes — dense pastries filled with lotus paste, red bean, or salted egg yolk. The festival's mythology converges on the figure of Chang'e, the Moon Goddess, whose ascent to the lunar palace following her inadvertent consumption of an immortality elixir is recounted in numerous variant versions across different Chinese literary and folk traditions. Yet beneath the romantic and mythological surface, the festival encodes a precise engagement with agricultural time: the full moon of the eighth month traditionally marked the conclusion of the autumn harvest, making collective celebration an expression of gratitude and communal solidarity rather than mere aesthetic appreciation of the celestial spectacle.", "What is perhaps most striking about the system of Chinese traditional festivals, viewed as a whole, is not the antiquity of any individual observance but the dynamic relationship between preservation and transformation that characterizes the tradition overall. Festivals have been suppressed, revived, commercialized, digitized, and reinterpreted across successive historical eras — from the iconoclasm of the Cultural Revolution to the contemporary commodification driven by domestic tourism and global brand partnerships. Scholars such as Stephan Feuchtwang have argued that the resilience of these festivals reflects not rigidity but a form of adaptive vitality: the capacity to absorb new meanings, technologies, and social contexts without surrendering the core ritual logic that makes participation feel continuous with the past. Whether this adaptive capacity will prove sufficient to sustain meaningful cultural transmission in an era of accelerating globalization and demographic shift remains, as yet, an open and genuinely consequential question.", "For the millions who observe these festivals — whether in ancestral villages, urban apartments, or diaspora communities thousands of miles from China — the question of authenticity may be less pressing than it appears to outside analysts. The act of gathering, of preparing and sharing specific foods, of acknowledging the dead and welcoming the new, carries its own pragmatic justification: it constitutes one of the primary means by which identity, memory, and belonging are reproduced across time in the absence of a single authoritative institution mandating compliance."], questions: [{ q: "Which of the following best captures the central argument of the passage?", options: ["Chinese traditional festivals function as complex, adaptive cultural systems that encode layered historical and social meanings while demonstrating an ongoing capacity to evolve across changing contexts.", "The commercialization and digitization of Chinese festivals have fundamentally altered their ritual significance, making authentic participation increasingly difficult in contemporary settings.", "Chinese traditional festivals have survived historical disruptions primarily because of government-sponsored cultural preservation programs and educational initiatives.", "The major Chinese festivals — including the Lunar New Year, Qingming, and the Mid-Autumn Festival — share a common origin in ancient agricultural calendars tied to the lunar cycle."], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, what is the significance of the color red during the Lunar New Year celebrations?", options: ["It reflects the traditional association between the color red and imperial authority in pre-modern Chinese culture.", "It commemorates the historical sacrifices of ancestors whose blood was believed to protect future generations.", "It represents the agricultural prosperity associated with the spring harvest season and the warming of the earth.", "It is linked to the symbolic warding off of a mythological creature that was said to attack communities annually."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, contemporary sociologists argue that the Qingming festival performs which two functions simultaneously?", options: ["It reinforces the practice of ancestor veneration while also encouraging younger generations to engage with traditional agricultural knowledge.", "It connects dispersed diaspora communities to shared cultural origins while also promoting national identity through state-sponsored rituals.", "It provides a structured context for the collective processing of grief while also strengthening intergenerational familial bonds.", "It preserves the physical infrastructure of ancestral burial sites while also transmitting folk religious beliefs to urban populations."], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"ascribed\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["prescribed as a mandatory requirement by religious institutions and ceremonial authorities", "inscribed permanently into written historical records and official commemorative texts", "documented through scholarly research and validated by comparative ethnographic evidence", "attributed or assigned as an inherent quality or characteristic to something"], answer: 3 }, { q: "Which of the following square brackets [1] , [2] , [3] , or [4] best indicates where the following sentence could be added? 'This multiplicity of origin narratives reflects a broader pattern in which official commemorative traditions and regional folk practices have long coexisted within the same festival framework without resolving into a single authoritative version.'", options: ["[1]", "[2]", "[3]", "[4]"], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, what do the actions of throwing zòngzi and racing boats at the Dragon Boat Festival originally commemorate?", options: ["The military victory of a Warring States general whose sacrifice prevented a regional invasion from succeeding.", "The seasonal rites performed to drive away malevolent forces believed to proliferate during the fifth lunar month.", "The community's attempt to rescue and protect the body of a loyal minister who drowned in an act of political protest.", "The gratitude shown to river deities whose protection was credited with ensuring a successful spring fishing season."], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"fuses\" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["gradually transforms one cultural tradition into an entirely different set of ritual practices over time", "formally institutionalizes previously informal practices by embedding them within a codified ceremonial structure", "deliberately conceals the contradictions between competing interpretations of a shared cultural event", "combines or merges distinct elements into a unified whole that retains multiple layers of meaning"], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, what does the timing of the Mid-Autumn Festival reveal about its underlying cultural significance?", options: ["Its occurrence at the conclusion of the autumn harvest indicates that the festival's communal dimension is rooted in agricultural gratitude rather than purely aesthetic appreciation.", "Its scheduling on the night of the full moon reflects an ancient cosmological belief that the moon's energy was at its most beneficial for ritual efficacy.", "Its alignment with the lunar calendar's eighth month demonstrates the sophisticated astronomical knowledge possessed by early Chinese agrarian societies.", "Its association with the Chang'e mythology suggests that the festival originally served as a rite of passage marking the transition from summer to the winter growing cycle."], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as part of the ritual structure of the Lunar New Year?", options: ["Decorating doorways with written couplets that express wishes for good fortune in the coming year.", "Preparing and sharing a reunion meal on the eve of the new year with immediate and extended family members.", "Presenting offerings of mooncakes and seasonal fruit at household altars dedicated to ancestral spirits.", "Distributing red envelopes containing monetary gifts as a symbolic gesture of protection and prosperity."], answer: 2 }, { q: "What can be inferred about the author's view of Chinese traditional festivals' capacity to survive ongoing globalization and demographic change?", options: ["The author suggests that the survival of Chinese traditional festivals depends primarily on the willingness of diaspora communities to maintain practices that mainland populations are increasingly abandoning.", "The author implies that commercialization and digital mediation have already compromised the cultural authenticity of Chinese festivals to a degree that makes long-term meaningful transmission unlikely.", "The author is confident that Chinese traditional festivals will endure without significant alteration because their core ritual logic has already demonstrated resilience across millennia of historical disruption.", "The author expresses cautious, qualified uncertainty — acknowledging the adaptive strengths of these festivals while leaving genuinely open the question of whether such adaptability will be adequate to future challenges."], answer: 3 }] },
  ] },
  { id: "rd-141", num: 141, title: "Đề 141", timeMin: 60, parts: [
    { title: "How Social Media Has Changed the Way We Connect", paragraphs: ["Twenty years ago, keeping in touch with friends who lived far away usually meant a phone call, a letter, or an occasional visit. Today, social media has made staying connected much easier. With just a few taps on a phone, people can send messages, share photos, and see what their friends and family are doing, no matter where in the world they are. This convenience has become such a normal part of daily life that many people check their social media accounts multiple times a day without even thinking about it.", "One of the biggest benefits of social media is that it helps people build and maintain relationships. Someone who moves to a new city for work or study can still feel close to old friends by commenting on their posts or sending quick messages. Families that are spread across different countries can share important moments, such as birthdays or graduations, almost instantly. For many people, social media has become a way to feel less alone, especially during times when meeting in person is difficult.", "Social media has also changed the way businesses operate. Small shops and local businesses now use platforms to advertise their products without spending large amounts of money on traditional advertising. A baker in a small town, for example, can post photos of fresh bread every morning and reach hundreds of potential customers nearby. Larger companies use social media to answer customer questions quickly and to build a friendly public image. This shift has given smaller businesses a chance to compete with bigger companies in ways that were not possible before.", "However, social media use also comes with certain problems. Many users report feeling more anxious or dissatisfied after spending long periods scrolling through other people's posts, since it is easy to compare one's own life to the carefully chosen, positive moments that others choose to share. Spending too much time on social media can also take time away from sleep, schoolwork, or face-to-face conversations. Doctors and teachers have started to encourage young people especially to set daily limits on how much time they spend on these platforms.", "Another issue is the spread of false information. Because anyone can post anything, incorrect news or misleading claims can spread very quickly before they are corrected. This has made it more important than ever for users to check whether a source is trustworthy before believing or sharing what they read. Some platforms have started adding warning labels to posts that contain unverified claims, though this system is still far from perfect.", "Despite these challenges, social media does not appear to be going away anytime soon. Instead, it continues to evolve , adding new features such as short videos, live streaming, and online shopping directly through apps. Whether these changes will solve the existing problems or create new ones remains to be seen, but it is clear that social media will remain a major part of how people communicate for years to come."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main idea of the passage?", options: ["Social media is mainly used by businesses to advertise products.", "Social media has completely replaced phone calls and letters as a way to communicate.", "Doctors recommend that everyone stop using social media entirely.", "Social media offers real benefits for relationships and business, but also brings challenges such as anxiety and false information."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, how can someone who moves to a new city stay close to old friends?", options: ["By visiting them in person every month.", "By commenting on their posts or sending quick messages.", "By calling them on the phone every day.", "By writing letters through the mail."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, what example is given of a small business using social media?", options: ["A large company opening new stores in different cities.", "A baker posting photos of fresh bread every morning.", "A shop hiring more employees to answer phone calls.", "A business paying for expensive television advertisements."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, why do many users feel more anxious after using social media?", options: ["They spend too much money on online shopping.", "They cannot find enough interesting content to watch.", "They receive too many messages from friends.", "They compare their own lives to the carefully chosen, positive moments others share."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, what have some platforms started doing about false information?", options: ["Banning all users who post news.", "Adding warning labels to posts with unverified claims.", "Charging a fee to share news articles.", "Deleting every post that mentions current events."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a problem linked to social media use?", options: ["Feeling more anxious or dissatisfied", "The spread of false information", "The high cost of using social media apps", "Less time for sleep and face-to-face conversation"], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"convenience\" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["expense", "ease", "confusion", "danger"], answer: 1 }, { q: "The word \"evolve\" in paragraph 6 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["disappear", "develop", "shrink", "repeat"], answer: 1 }, { q: "The word \"they\" in paragraph 5 refers to _______.", options: ["platforms", "incorrect news or misleading claims", "warning labels", "users"], answer: 1 }, { q: "What can be inferred about the future of social media platforms?", options: ["They will completely remove all features related to sharing personal photos.", "They will be banned by governments because of the anxiety they cause.", "They will likely stop adding new features to focus only on fixing existing problems.", "They will probably need to balance adding new features with addressing concerns about user wellbeing."], answer: 3 }] },
    { title: "Choosing the Right Seeds for a Successful Harvest", paragraphs: ["For farmers and home gardeners alike, the success of an entire growing season often depends on decisions made before a single seed touches the soil. Selecting the right seeds is one of the most important steps in agriculture, yet it is frequently underestimated by beginners who assume that any seed labeled for a given plant will perform equally well. In reality, seed selection involves weighing several interconnected factors, including climate suitability, soil conditions, disease resistance, and the intended purpose of the harvest.", "Climate compatibility is generally considered the starting point for any seed selection process. Seeds that thrive in a cool, temperate region may struggle or fail entirely if planted in a hot, humid climate, and the reverse is equally true. Experienced growers typically consult regional planting guides or local agricultural extension offices to determine which varieties have a proven track record in their specific area. Ignoring this step can result in poor germination rates, stunted growth, or crops that never mature enough to be harvested at all.", "Beyond climate, the choice between hybrid and heirloom seeds represents another significant decision point. Hybrid seeds are bred by crossing two different parent plants to combine desirable traits such as higher yield, uniform size, or resistance to specific pests. Heirloom seeds, by contrast, are open-pollinated varieties passed down over generations, often prized for their distinctive flavor or historical value, though they may lack the disease resistance bred into modern hybrids. Farmers growing crops for commercial sale frequently favor hybrids for their predictability, while home gardeners interested in preserving biodiversity sometimes prefer heirlooms despite the additional risk.", "Soil condition plays an equally decisive role, since certain seeds require specific pH levels, drainage capabilities, or nutrient profiles to germinate successfully. A grower who fails to test soil composition before selecting seeds risks investing time and money into a crop poorly matched to the land available. Simple soil testing kits, now widely available and inexpensive, allow even small-scale gardeners to identify deficiencies and choose seed varieties accordingly, or to amend the soil before planting begins.", "Disease and pest resistance has become an increasingly prominent consideration as growers face mounting pressure from evolving pathogens and insect populations. Seed companies now routinely label packets with resistance codes indicating which specific diseases a variety can withstand, information that can prove decisive for growers in regions with a history of particular crop illnesses. Relying on resistant varieties can substantially reduce the need for chemical treatments later in the growing cycle, offering both economic and environmental advantages.", "Finally, the intended purpose of the harvest should guide seed selection as much as any environmental factor. A tomato variety bred for long-distance shipping, with thick skin designed to withstand transport, will generally taste noticeably different from one bred purely for fresh, local consumption. Gardeners growing food primarily for their own table often prioritize flavor and nutritional value over the durability that commercial growers require, illustrating how the same crop can call for entirely different seed choices depending on the end goal."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main idea of the passage?", options: ["Choosing the right seeds requires weighing several interconnected factors, including climate, soil, disease resistance, and the intended purpose of the harvest.", "Only commercial farmers need to think carefully about which seeds to plant.", "Soil testing kits have made all other seed selection factors unnecessary.", "Hybrid seeds are always a better choice than heirloom seeds for every grower."], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, what can happen if a grower ignores climate compatibility when selecting seeds?", options: ["The soil will automatically become more fertile.", "The seeds will always grow faster than expected.", "Poor germination rates, stunted growth, or crops that never fully mature.", "The plants will develop stronger resistance to pests."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, why do farmers growing crops for commercial sale frequently favor hybrid seeds?", options: ["Hybrids are always cheaper to purchase than heirloom seeds.", "Hybrids require no soil testing before planting.", "Hybrids are valued for their predictability, such as higher yield and uniform size.", "Hybrids are the only seeds legally permitted for commercial farming."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what allows small-scale gardeners to identify soil deficiencies?", options: ["Waiting until the crop fails to determine what went wrong.", "Consulting only with seed companies directly.", "Hiring a professional agricultural consultant for every planting season.", "Simple soil testing kits that are now widely available and inexpensive."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, what can relying on disease-resistant seed varieties help reduce?", options: ["The overall size of the harvest.", "The need for chemical treatments later in the growing cycle.", "The cost of purchasing soil testing kits.", "The amount of sunlight the crop requires."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a factor influencing seed selection?", options: ["Soil conditions", "The color of the seed packaging", "Climate suitability", "Disease resistance"], answer: 1 }, { q: "The word \"decisive\" in paragraph 5 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["confusing", "optional", "final", "important"], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"amend\" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["test", "ignore", "replace", "improve"], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"one\" in paragraph 6 refers to _______.", options: ["thick skin", "long-distance shipping", "a tomato variety bred purely for fresh, local consumption", "commercial growers"], answer: 2 }, { q: "What can be inferred about home gardeners compared to commercial farmers?", options: ["Home gardeners are legally required to grow only heirloom varieties.", "Home gardeners and commercial farmers always choose identical seed varieties.", "Home gardeners generally prioritize flavor and personal preference, while commercial farmers prioritize predictability and durability for transport.", "Home gardeners never consider disease resistance when selecting seeds."], answer: 2 }] },
    { title: "A Small Chè Shop in Phú Yên and the Economics of Culinary Tradition", paragraphs: ["Tucked along a narrow lane in Tuy Hòa, the coastal capital of Phú Yên province, a modest dessert shop run by a woman known locally simply as Cô Phương has, over nearly three decades, become something of an unofficial landmark. [1] The shop serves chè, a category of sweet soups and puddings ubiquitous across Vietnam, yet what distinguishes Cô Phương's establishment is not novelty but an almost obstinate adherence to methods her mother taught her, methods that predate the arrival of refrigeration to the neighbourhood and that she has, by her own admission, refused to meaningfully alter since.", "Economically, the shop occupies a curious position that local business researchers have found instructive precisely because it defies conventional expansion logic. Cô Phương has been offered, on multiple documented occasions, opportunities to franchise her recipes or supply pre-packaged versions to regional supermarket chains, proposals that would almost certainly have generated substantially greater revenue than her single, twelve-seat shopfront currently produces. [2] She has declined each offer, citing concerns that mass production would necessarily compromise the freshness of ingredients such as mung beans and pandan leaves, which she sources daily rather than in bulk, and which she maintains lose their characteristic aroma within hours of preparation.", "This resistance to scaling, researchers argue, should not be mistaken for a simple lack of business acumen. Interviews conducted with the shop's regular patrons reveal that a considerable proportion travel from outside Tuy Hòa specifically because the chè is understood to be unreproducible elsewhere, a scarcity that paradoxically sustains rather than limits demand. Several economists studying small-scale food enterprises in central Vietnam have cited the shop as an example of what one study termed reputational capital substituting for physical expansion, wherein a business's value derives precisely from its refusal to grow beyond a scale at which quality can be personally guaranteed.", "Nevertheless, the shop's long-term viability remains a subject of genuine uncertainty among those who have studied it closely. Cô Phương, now in her early sixties, has no children interested in continuing the trade, and the intricate, largely undocumented techniques involved in balancing sweetness, texture, and the precise timing of each ingredient's addition exist almost entirely as embodied knowledge rather than written recipe. [3] Some observers have proposed that an apprenticeship model, in which a trusted employee gradually assumes responsibility for recipe decisions, might preserve continuity, though Cô Phương herself has expressed skepticism that anyone outside her immediate family could replicate the intuitive judgments the process requires.", "The shop's situation illustrates a broader tension confronting small culinary businesses throughout Vietnam's coastal provinces, where tourism-driven demand for what might be termed authentic local cuisine sits uneasily alongside the economic pressures that typically favour standardisation and growth. [4] Tourism boards in several provinces have begun promoting such establishments precisely for their resistance to commercialisation, an approach that risks a certain irony: the more successfully a shop's scarcity is marketed, the greater the pressure it faces to expand in order to meet the very demand that scarcity generated.", "Whatever becomes of Cô Phương's shop in the coming years, its trajectory offers a case study in a question with implications well beyond Phú Yên: whether traditions dependent on an individual's uncompromising standards can survive the transition to a subsequent generation without either diluting into something more conventional or disappearing altogether once that individual is no longer able to continue."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main idea of the passage?", options: ["Cô Phương's small chè shop deliberately resists expansion in favour of preserving quality and reputational value, though its long-term survival beyond her own involvement remains uncertain.", "Cô Phương's chè shop is failing financially due to poor management decisions.", "Tourism boards in Phú Yên have forced Cô Phương to commercialise her recipes.", "Franchising traditional Vietnamese desserts is always more profitable than running a single small shop."], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, what has Cô Phương declined on multiple occasions?", options: ["Invitations to appear on television cooking shows.", "Offers to franchise her recipes or supply pre-packaged versions to supermarket chains.", "Government subsidies for small food businesses.", "Requests from customers to change her recipe."], answer: 1 }, { q: "According to the passage, what concept do economists use to describe the shop's business model?", options: ["Vertical integration of the supply chain.", "Seasonal pricing adjustment.", "Aggressive market penetration.", "Reputational capital substituting for physical expansion."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, why is the shop's long-term viability uncertain?", options: ["Cô Phương plans to retire and close the shop within the year.", "Local authorities have threatened to revoke the shop's operating license.", "Cô Phương has no children interested in continuing the trade, and her techniques exist mainly as embodied, undocumented knowledge.", "The shop has lost its lease and must relocate."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what irony do tourism boards' promotional efforts risk creating?", options: ["Local competitors may be forced to close permanently.", "Tourism boards may lose funding from provincial governments.", "The more successfully a shop's scarcity is marketed, the greater the pressure it faces to expand and meet that generated demand.", "Tourists may stop visiting Phú Yên altogether."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a reason Cô Phương resists expanding her business?", options: ["A lack of investment capital to fund expansion.", "Concern that mass production would compromise ingredient freshness.", "A belief that daily-sourced ingredients lose their aroma quickly.", "Doubt that anyone outside her family could replicate her intuitive judgments."], answer: 0 }, { q: "The word \"obstinate\" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["flexible", "careless", "uncertain", "stubborn"], answer: 3 }, { q: "The word \"viability\" in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["profitability", "popularity", "sustainability", "originality"], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"it\" in paragraph 5 refers to _______.", options: ["central Vietnam", "tourism-driven demand", "a shop", "standardisation"], answer: 2 }, { q: "Which of the following square brackets [1] , [2] , [3] , or [4] best indicates where the following sentence could be added? 'Similar establishments elsewhere that accepted comparable offers, researchers note, often saw customer loyalty erode within a few years of expansion.'", options: ["[4]", "[2]", "[3]", "[1]"], answer: 2 }] },
    { title: "The Hadza and the Anthropological Debate over 'Pristine' Foraging Societies", paragraphs: ["Among the last remaining populations to derive the majority of their caloric intake from hunting and gathering rather than agriculture, the Hadza of northern Tanzania have occupied an outsized position in anthropological literature, one that some contemporary researchers now argue has produced as much distortion as insight. Numbering only a few thousand individuals concentrated around Lake Eyasi, the Hadza have been studied intensively since the mid-twentieth century, frequently invoked in popular and academic writing alike as a living window onto the subsistence strategies that characterised the vast majority of human history prior to the advent of farming.", "This framing, several anthropologists have come to argue, rests on an assumption that does not withstand close scrutiny: that a foraging society observed in the present day can be treated as functionally equivalent to Paleolithic populations, effectively frozen in time and untouched by the intervening millennia. Critics of this view note that the Hadza have, in fact, interacted with pastoralist and agricultural neighbours for centuries, have periodically incorporated cultivated foods into their diet, and have had their territory and mobility substantially reshaped by colonial and postcolonial land policies. Treating contemporary Hadza subsistence patterns as a direct proxy for deep prehistory, these researchers contend, risks obscuring rather than illuminating the actual diversity of ancestral human lifeways.", "Proponents of continued Hadza-focused research counter that this critique , while methodologically valid, should not be taken to imply that such research lacks value; rather, it suggests that findings must be interpreted with considerably more caution than earlier generations of researchers exercised. Data drawn from Hadza foraging patterns, gut microbiome composition, and activity levels have proven genuinely useful, they argue, not as a literal snapshot of Paleolithic life but as one data point among several non-agricultural societies that, taken collectively, can help constrain hypotheses about the plausible range of ancestral human behaviour. The distinction between the Hadza as a direct analogue and the Hadza as one useful comparative case is, in this view, precisely the nuance that popular science writing has frequently failed to preserve.", "A further complication concerns the ethical dimensions of the research relationship itself. Decades of visits from academic researchers, documentary film crews, and increasingly, adventure tourists seeking an authentic glimpse of hunter-gatherer life have arguably altered the very behaviours being studied, a phenomenon some social scientists term observer-induced change. Hadza individuals interviewed in recent studies have reported adapting their presentation of daily activities in ways they believe researchers or visitors expect to see, raising uncomfortable questions about how much of the published record reflects unmediated practice versus performance shaped by decades of external attention.", "Tanzanian land policy adds another layer of urgency to these debates. Government initiatives promoting settled agriculture and, at various points, wildlife conservation zones have progressively restricted the territory available for traditional Hadza foraging, a pressure that has pushed some community members toward wage labour, tourism-related employment, or partial reliance on purchased food. Whether these shifts represent a gradual erosion of a viable alternative subsistence strategy or an inevitable, perhaps even overdue, transition remains a matter on which the Hadza themselves are reportedly divided, with older residents generally expressing greater attachment to traditional foraging than younger community members who have grown up with greater exposure to the national economy.", "What emerges from this body of scholarship, taken as a whole, is not a straightforward story of an untouched people offering a direct portal into humanity's ancestral past, but rather a considerably more complicated picture: a population whose foraging knowledge remains genuinely significant to anthropological understanding, even as the conditions under which that knowledge is studied, and the very practices being observed, have themselves been substantially shaped by the decades of outside attention the Hadza have received precisely because of their perceived rarity."], questions: [{ q: "What is the main idea of the passage?", options: ["Anthropologists have unanimously agreed to stop studying the Hadza due to ethical concerns.", "The Hadza have never had any contact with neighbouring agricultural or pastoralist societies.", "Research on the Hadza remains genuinely valuable, but treating them as an unchanged window into Paleolithic life oversimplifies a more complicated reality shaped by centuries of contact and decades of external attention.", "Tanzanian government policy has completely eliminated traditional Hadza foraging practices."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what have critics noted about the Hadza's historical interactions?", options: ["They have interacted with pastoralist and agricultural neighbours for centuries and incorporated cultivated foods into their diet.", "They have remained completely isolated from all neighbouring groups for millennia.", "They have had no contact with colonial or postcolonial land policies.", "They abandoned foraging entirely in favour of agriculture centuries ago."], answer: 0 }, { q: "According to the passage, how do proponents of continued Hadza research argue the data should be used?", options: ["As a literal, unquestionable snapshot of Paleolithic life.", "As evidence that all foraging societies behave identically.", "As proof that agriculture never significantly altered human diets.", "As one useful comparative data point among several non-agricultural societies, rather than a direct analogue."], answer: 3 }, { q: "According to the passage, what have some Hadza individuals reported doing when researchers or visitors are present?", options: ["Demanding payment before allowing any observation to occur.", "Refusing to participate in any studies or interviews.", "Adapting their presentation of daily activities in ways they believe observers expect to see.", "Relocating permanently to avoid contact with outsiders."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, what pressure has Tanzanian land policy placed on some Hadza community members?", options: ["It has banned all forms of outside research permanently.", "It has required all Hadza to relocate to urban centres immediately.", "It has pushed some toward wage labour, tourism-related employment, or reliance on purchased food.", "It has granted the Hadza significantly more land than they previously held."], answer: 2 }, { q: "According to the passage, which of the following is NOT mentioned as a factor that has altered traditional Hadza life?", options: ["A major natural disaster that destroyed Hadza territory.", "Government land policies promoting agriculture and conservation zones.", "Centuries of interaction with pastoralist and agricultural neighbours.", "Decades of attention from researchers, film crews, and tourists."], answer: 0 }, { q: "The word \"proxy\" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["obstacle", "critique", "substitute", "origin"], answer: 2 }, { q: "The word \"erosion\" in paragraph 5 is closest in meaning to _______.", options: ["gradual decline", "sudden collapse", "expansion", "renewal"], answer: 0 }, { q: "The phrase \"this critique\" in paragraph 3 refers to _______.", options: ["the suggestion that all anthropological research should be banned", "the observation about tourist behaviour", "the claim that Hadza gut microbiome data is inaccurate", "the argument that treating contemporary Hadza patterns as a direct proxy for prehistory risks obscuring true diversity"], answer: 3 }, { q: "What can be inferred about the future of traditional Hadza foraging practices?", options: ["It has already been fully replaced by wage labour for the entire community.", "Its trajectory likely depends partly on generational differences in attachment to tradition, alongside continuing external pressures on land and lifestyle.", "It is completely unaffected by any generational or policy-related factors.", "It will almost certainly disappear within the next year regardless of any factors."], answer: 1 }] },
  ] },
];
